#> tool: awkrepl
#> wait: 10 :Mark
#> pause: 40
#> must: 1 :Beth    4.00  0
#> must: 4 :Mark    5.00  20
#> not: 11 :
#> source: ++a
# 3. Number only the non-blank lines. Pement: awk 'NF{$0=++a " :" $0};{print}'
# NF is the number of fields; a blank line has 0, which is false as a pattern.
# ++a increments our own counter before use. Assigning to $0 rewrites the line.
# Twelve lines, ten of them non-blank, so the numbers stop at 10.
# Try: swap the order of the two rules and see why that breaks it.
NF{$0=++a " :" $0};{print}

#DATA
Beth    4.00  0
Dan     3.75  0
Kathy   4.00  10

Mark    5.00  20
Mary    5.50  22
Susie   4.25  18
Susie   4.25  18
